      "name": "saturation-meta-merge",
      "title": "Saturation meta-merge — drain the queue when the runners are full",
      "description": "When the CI runners have been full for a long time, drain a repository's ready PRs in one step: hold the swarm, cancel the queued PR runs, stack every admitted PR onto one meta-merge branch with merge commits, and land that branch on `main` without waiting for CI, on the owner's card that names each PR. Then re-run main's checks and report. Use for \"runners are full\", \"cancel everything and merge what's ready\", \"meta-merge\", \"consolidate the queue\", and when the queue has not moved for an hour or more.",
